Why Is Demand Increasing
Sub-5nm Semiconductor Demand: Advanced logic and memory architectures require highly precise plasma etching to maintain critical dimensions and minimize process-related defects.
Advanced Packaging Growth: Chiplets, 3D ICs, TSVs, and interposers are increasing demand for specialized deep-silicon and high-aspect-ratio etching capabilities.
AI-Driven Process Control: Machine-learning-enabled recipe optimization and real-time process monitoring are helping fabs improve cycle times, yield, and defect control.

Semiconductor Manufacturing Watch: Atomic-Scale Etching
The industry is moving toward increasingly selective and precise etching processes as semiconductor structures become smaller and more complex. Atomic Layer Etching, selective chemistry development, advanced plasma sources, real-time endpoint detection, and AI-enhanced process control are among the technologies shaping next-generation etch systems.

