Why This Market Matters
Semiconductor etch equipment is essential for selectively removing material layers from wafers and creating the structures required for advanced electronic devices. As transistor geometries shrink and memory architectures become more complex, equipment suppliers are developing systems capable of greater selectivity, profile control, uniformity, and process automation.

